      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The functional L changes basis from recurrence polynomials to monomial moments; the Hankel matrix then packages pairwise moment information into determinant invariants. This representation exposes prime-factor behavior and permits comparison with binomial moment sequences, but matching initial determinant data is weaker than a structural identity or product formula.",
