      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "When endpoint geometry leaves non-identity non-intersecting matchings after ordinary tail switching, the paper first applies a problem-specific sign-reversing involution to remove an extra boundary or symmetry class, then applies standard intersection cancellation; the survivors are positive fixed-point path families counted by the determinant.",
