    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b7c7700af8e6edc216dc6187984c7789c44626c44ba0d0872e332f80c1c879bf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Positive three-term orthogonality forces simple real interlacing zeros, but the four-term functional loses cross-orthogonality. The special normalized recurrence nevertheless interlaces for C≥3 by an independent continuity/characteristic-root argument and has a positive moment representation, while a Hermite-based four-term construction preserves functional positivity yet gives q_4 a non-real zero.",
