    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f85252f81f8f907680533f4f6c552c8b8dac827ab7749cfd9c9fb1b493730705",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The recurrence moments form a common invariant represented by inverse coefficient entries, weighted excursions, 2–3 trees, Lagrange coefficients, multinomial sums, contour jumps, and positive real densities. At C=3, substitutions give beta and fractional-binomial forms, while inserting the one-variable moments into the Hankel determinant and antisymmetrizing produces a squared-Vandermonde multiple integral and then explicit binomial Hankel entries.",
